<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Worker">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    THE API'S appsettings.json IS THE ONE THAT SHIPS.

    ClimateTracking.Api references this project so one container is both the API and the
    scheduler (#219). Both projects carry an appsettings.json at their root, and both
    want to land at /app/publish/appsettings.json, so `dotnet publish` of the API failed
    outright with NETSDK1152 — which meant the deploy path added for #219 could not
    build at all. Nothing caught it because deploy-tracking-prod.yml is a deploy
    workflow, not a PR check: no pull request has ever built this image.

    Excluded rather than suppressed with ErrorOnDuplicatePublishOutputFiles. That flag
    lets the SDK pick a winner, and the file below is a DEVELOPMENT config: a localhost
    connection string with a placeholder password, and three deliberately blank required
    values. Shipping it as the production appsettings.json would be strictly worse than
    the build error, and non-deterministically so.

    Nothing is lost. Co-hosted, the workers read IConfiguration from the API's host,
    which is the API's appsettings.json plus the container's environment. This file
    serves only ClimateTracking.Workers' own standalone Program.cs, and that host is
    kept unbuilt as the documented opt-out (see ClimateTracking.Api.csproj) precisely
    because App Runner needs something that binds a port.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Content Update="appsettings*.json" CopyToPublishDirectory="Never" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting" Version="10.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore" Version="10.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Npgsql.EntityFrameworkCore.PostgreSQL" Version="10.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\ClimateTracking.Application\ClimateTracking.Application.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\ClimateTracking.Infrastructure\ClimateTracking.Infrastructure.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
